   "is_new": true,
   "source": {
    "label": "thm:main",
    "number": "Theorem (thm:main)",
    "quote": "There exists a universal constant $C>0$ such that the following holds. Let $T\\ge1$ be an integer, let $\\delta\\in(0,1)$, and assume $1\\le m\\le d-1$. Run \\Cref{alg:exp3-kw}. Then, with probability at least $1-\\delta$, \\[ R_T \\le C\\sqrt{ dT\\left( \\log K+\\log\\frac1\\delta \\right) }, \\] where $K=\\binom{d}{m}$. One may take $C=160$."
   },
   "confidence": "high",
   "notes": "Realized regret bound w.p. 1-delta. Polynomial time per Proposition (prop:efficient-implementation): T*poly(d,m,log T) time, poly(d,m) space. Equivalent to O_tilde(sqrt(d s T)), s=min(m,d-m). Theorem numbering counter conflicts with appendix 'Theorem 1', so label used."
  },
