    "quote": "There exist universal constants $c>0$ and $\\delta_0\\in(0,1)$ and a threshold $\\mathfrak T(d,m,\\delta)$ bounded by a polynomial in $d$, $m$, and $\\log(1/\\delta)$ such that the following holds. Let $d\\ge2$, $1\\le m\\le d-1$, $\\delta\\in(0,\\delta_0]$, and $T\\ge\\mathfrak T(d,m,\\delta)$. For every randomized policy on $\\cX_{d,m}$, there exists a deterministic adaptive non-anticipating loss process whose action losses belong to $[0,1]$ and such that \\[ \\Pp ( R_T\\ge c\\sqrt{dT(\\log\\binom dm+\\log\\frac1\\delta)} )\\ge\\delta. \\]"
   },
   "confidence": "high",
   "notes": "Lower bound holding with probability at least delta (tail lower bound)."
